<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-BBB-</p>
<p>Taisei Corp, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002</p>
<p>Tetsugen Corp (unlisted), 20 million mark unsecured due 2001, private placement, guaranteed by Long-Term Credit Bank of Japan  </p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>Mitsubishi Chemical Corp,</p>
<p>20 billion yen unsecured due 2004</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2007</p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Kobe Steel Ltd,</p>
<p>five billion yen unsecured due 2001</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2009</p>
<p>Tietech Co Ltd, 156 million yen unsecured with warrants due 2001  </p>
<p>-CCC-</p>
<p>Diamond Lease Co Ltd, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2002</p>
</text>
